<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, maximum-scale=5.0, minimum-scale=1.0">
    <meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="ie=edge">
    <meta name="Description" content="About Dwayne Codling — Head of Development at Foundation Commerce, people-first leader, D&I advocate, and powerlifter based in Nottingham.">
    <meta name="keywords" content="about, leadership, experience, D&I, powerlifting">
    <title>About Me — Dwayne Codling</title>
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="About Me — Dwayne Codling" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Head of Development. People-first leader. D&I advocate." />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://dwaynecodling.com/assets/img/share/dwayne-share-about.jpg" />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://dwaynecodling.com/about-me" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://dwaynecodling.com/about-me" />
    <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Person",
      "name": "Dwayne Codling",
      "url": "https://dwaynecodling.com",
      "jobTitle": "Head of Development",
      "description": "Head of Development, people-first leader, and D&I advocate based in Nottingham.",
      "image": "https://dwaynecodling.com/assets/img/share/dwayne-share-about.jpg",
      "sameAs": [
        "https://x.com/codling",
        "https://www.linkedin.com/in/dwayne-codling/",
        "https://github.com/dwaynecodling",
        "https://www.instagram.com/dwaynecodling.fitness"
      ]
    }
    </script>
    <%- include("../partials/links") %>
    <style>
        .about-hero {
            background-color: #162419;
            border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(200,133,58,0.15);
            padding: 8rem 0 6rem;
        }

        .about-intro {
            display: grid;
            gap: 4rem;
            align-items: start;
            margin-bottom: 0;
        }

        @media (min-width: 62em) {
            .about-intro {
                grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.4fr;
                gap: 8rem;
            }
        }

        .about-intro__image {
            position: relative;
        }

        .about-intro__img {
            width: 100%;
            aspect-ratio: 3/4;
            object-fit: cover;
            object-position: center top;
            display: block;
        }

        .about-intro__label {
            font-size: 1.2rem;
            font-weight: 600;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 0.2em;
            color: #c8853a;
            margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
        }

        .about-intro__heading {
            font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif;
            font-size: var(--heading-2);
            font-weight: 700;
            color: #f4ede0;
            line-height: 1.2;
            margin-bottom: 2.4rem;
        }

        .about-intro__text {
            font-size: 1.7rem;
            line-height: 3rem;
            color: #a89e90;
            margin-bottom: 2rem;
        }

        .about-intro__links {
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            gap: 1.2rem;
            list-style: none;
            margin-top: 3rem;
        }

        .about-intro__link a {
            display: inline-block;
            font-size: 1.3rem;
            font-weight: 600;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 0.1em;
            color: #c8853a;
            border: 1px solid rgba(200,133,58,0.4);
            padding: 0.8rem 1.8rem;
            border-radius: 99px;
            transition: all .2s;
        }

        .about-intro__link a:hover {
            background-color: #c8853a;
            color: #0d1a10;
        }

        .about-intro__link a:after { display: none; }

        /* Story section */
        .about-story {
            max-width: 74rem;
            margin: 0 auto;
        }

        .about-story__heading {
            font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif;
            font-size: var(--heading-3);
            font-weight: 700;
            color: #f4ede0;
            margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
            margin-top: 5rem;
            padding-top: 4rem;
            border-top: 1px solid rgba(200,133,58,0.15);
        }

        .about-story__heading:first-child {
            margin-top: 0;
            padding-top: 0;
            border-top: none;
        }

        .about-story__text {
            font-size: 1.7rem;
            line-height: 3.2rem;
            color: #a89e90;
            margin-bottom: 2rem;
        }

        .about-story__quote {
            font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif;
            font-size: 2.2rem;
            font-style: italic;
            color: #c8853a;
            border-left: 3px solid #c8853a;
            padding-left: 2.4rem;
            margin: 4rem 0;
            line-height: 1.5;
        }

        /* People grid */
        .people-section {
            margin-bottom: 10rem;
        }

        .people-section__label {
            font-size: 1.2rem;
            font-weight: 600;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 0.2em;
            color: #c8853a;
            margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
        }

        .people-section__heading {
            font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif;
            font-size: var(--heading-2);
            font-weight: 700;
            color: #f4ede0;
            margin-bottom: 4rem;
            max-width: 52rem;
        }

        .about-intro__img { border-radius: 2.4rem; height: auto; }
        .about-story a { color: #c8853a; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; text-decoration-color: rgba(200,133,58,0.4); }
        .about-story a:hover { color: #f4ede0; text-decoration-color: #c8853a; }
        .about-story a:after { display: none; }
        .people-feature { margin: 0; }
        .people-feature img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 3 / 2; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 1.6rem; }
        .people-feature__grid { display: grid; gap: 2rem; }
        @media (min-width: 48em) { .people-feature__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }

        .about-story__figure { margin: 4rem 0; }
        .about-story__figure img {
            display: block;
            width: 100%;
            border-radius: 1.6rem;
            aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
            object-fit: cover;
        }
        .about-story__figure--wide img { aspect-ratio: auto; height: auto; }
        .about-story__figure--portrait { max-width: 44rem; }
        .about-story__figure--portrait img { aspect-ratio: 4 / 5; height: auto; }
        .about-story__caption { margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 1.3rem; line-height: 1.6; color: #b3a99b; }
        .about-story__figure--pair { display: grid; gap: 1.6rem; }
        @media (min-width: 48em) {
            .about-story__figure--pair { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
            .about-story__figure--pair img { aspect-ratio: 1; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<%- include("../partials/nav") %>

<main id="main-content" class="content" role="main">

    <!-- Page Hero -->
    <section class="m-bottom-0">
        <div class="about-hero">
            <div class="container">
                <p class="page-header__label">About me</p>
                <h1 class="page-header__title">
                    People-first leader.<br>Always learning.
                </h1>
                <p class="page-header__description">
                    Head of Development at Foundation Commerce from Nottingham, originally from Jamaica. Over a decade building teams, bridging gaps, and trying to leave things better than I found them.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Intro with photo -->
    <section class="p-top-6">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="about-intro">
                <div class="about-intro__image">
                    <picture>
                        <source type="image/avif" srcset="/assets/img/pages/about-me/dwayne-portrait-about.avif">
                        <source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/img/pages/about-me/dwayne-portrait-about.webp">
                        <img class="about-intro__img" src="/assets/img/pages/about-me/dwayne-portrait-about.jpg" width="900" height="1200" alt="Dwayne Codling standing with his hands on his hips, smiling" fetchpriority="high" />
                    </picture>
                </div>
                <div class="about-intro__body">
                    <p class="about-intro__label">Head of Development</p>
                    <h2 class="about-intro__heading">Building teams that perform, and people who grow.</h2>
                    <p class="about-intro__text">
                        I've grown from frontend developer to director-level leader across some of the UK's leading digital agencies. Currently at Foundation Commerce, where I'm building and scaling the development team to deliver world-class solutions.
                    </p>
                    <p class="about-intro__text">
                        What drives me isn't the org chart; it's the people. Watching someone step into their potential, seeing a team click into gear, building a culture where people actually want to show up. That's what I'm here for.
                    </p>
                    <p class="about-intro__text">
                        My focus is on creating a development environment where technical excellence and people-first leadership go hand in hand.
                    </p>
                    <ul class="about-intro__links">
                        <li class="about-intro__link"><a href="#story">My story</a></li>
                        <li class="about-intro__link"><a href="#inclusion">D&I work</a></li>
                        <li class="about-intro__link"><a href="#people">People first</a></li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Story -->
    <section>
        <div class="container">
            <div class="about-story">

                <h3 id="story" class="about-story__heading">How did you get here?</h3>
                <p class="about-story__text">It started at university on a Multimedia course, where I discovered web design and development almost by accident. That curiosity never left. Over the years I built things, taught things, and grew more confident in both my craft and my ability to share it.</p>
                <p class="about-story__text">I spent four years as a Lecturer in Media at New College Nottingham, teaching students real-world frontend skills while running freelance projects on the side. Watching a student land their first industry job? That doesn't get old.</p>

                <h3 class="about-story__heading">The move into agency life</h3>
                <p class="about-story__text">I made the move into full-time agency development at JH in Nottingham, growing from frontend developer to Pod Lead, managing a team delivering large-scale eCommerce builds. That leadership role opened a door I didn't know I was walking toward. I discovered I was just as energised by developing people as I was by developing software.</p>

                <figure class="about-story__figure about-story__figure--pair">
                    <picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/img/pages/about-me/story/teaching.webp"><img src="/assets/img/pages/about-me/story/teaching.jpg" alt="Dwayne taking a selfie with students in a classroom" loading="lazy" /></picture>
                    <picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/img/pages/about-me/story/agency.webp"><img src="/assets/img/pages/about-me/story/agency.jpg" alt="Dwayne working alongside a colleague at a desk" loading="lazy" /></picture>
                </figure>

                <h3 class="about-story__heading">The IDHL chapter</h3>
                <p class="about-story__text">At IDHL I served first as Head of Development at Pinpoint, then as Development Director across the group. The brief: take five separate agencies, each with its own culture, and build one unified team. We established performance review structures, cross-team training programmes, and sustainable ways of working.</p>
                <p class="about-story__text">One highlight I'm proud of: a training initiative that helped Adobe Commerce developers upskill into Shopify, unlocking new career paths and expanding capability across the business.</p>

                <figure class="about-story__figure about-story__figure--wide">
                    <picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/img/pages/about-me/story/idhl-speech.webp"><img src="/assets/img/pages/about-me/story/idhl-speech.jpg" width="1200" height="900" alt="Dwayne speaking to the room at an IDHL team event, notes in hand, as a colleague laughs and claps" loading="lazy" /></picture>
                </figure>

                <h3 class="about-story__heading">Foundation Commerce</h3>
                <p class="about-story__text">In June 2026, I joined Foundation Commerce as Head of Development. This was a deliberate move to a business where I could build something from the ground up with intention. The focus here is different: scaling a high-performing development team that doesn't just ship code, but builds sustainable, people-centric engineering culture.</p>
                <p class="about-story__text">At Foundation Commerce, I'm responsible for team development, technical direction, and creating an environment where developers thrive. The mission is clear: hire exceptional talent, give them the tools and autonomy to do their best work, and build a team that genuinely enjoys what they do.</p>

                <figure class="about-story__figure about-story__figure--wide">
                    <picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/img/pages/about-me/story/foundation-stand.webp"><img src="/assets/img/pages/about-me/story/foundation-stand.jpg" width="1200" height="800" alt="Dwayne with two Foundation Commerce colleagues at the Foundation stand" loading="lazy" /></picture>
                    <figcaption class="about-story__caption">At the Foundation Commerce stand, eCommerce Expo London 2026. Photo: Hyv&auml;</figcaption>
                </figure>

                <h3 id="inclusion" class="about-story__heading">Diversity &amp; Inclusion</h3>
                <p class="about-story__text">This matters to me personally. I've spoken at Tech Nottingham, Drink Digital, HackSoc, and allyship events in Leeds. My view is simple: if we build products for a diverse world but refuse to invest in diverse talent, we're failing everyone.</p>
                <p class="about-story__text">I've also advised ProjectFunction, a programme creating pathways into tech for underrepresented groups. If I can help one person find their way in who might not have otherwise, that's a legacy worth having.</p>

                <div class="about-story__quote">
                    "Forward ever, backward never."
                </div>

                <h3 class="about-story__heading">Beyond work</h3>
                <p class="about-story__text">I'm a dad first. I do the school runs, read in class with the kids, show up at sports days. Family isn't something I fit around work; it's the reason I take my work seriously.</p>
                <figure class="about-story__figure about-story__figure--portrait">
                    <picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/img/pages/about-me/story/suit.webp"><img src="/assets/img/pages/about-me/story/suit.jpg" width="900" height="1125" alt="Dwayne smiling in a cream three-piece suit with a burgundy tie" loading="lazy" /></picture>
                </figure>
                <p class="about-story__text">I also compete in raw powerlifting. In March 2026 I entered my first WRPF competition and finished 2nd in my class with a 495kg total. In November, eight weeks after a rotator cuff injury, I totalled 522.5kg at Nottingham Strong. Training taught me something I already believed but needed to live: setbacks are part of the process. How you respond defines the outcome.</p>
                <p class="about-story__text">Read <a href="/post/nottingham-strong">how Nottingham Strong went</a>, or follow the training on <a href="https://www.instagram.com/dwaynecodling.fitness" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Instagram</a>.</p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- People First photo section -->
    <section id="people">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="people-section">
                <p class="people-section__label">People first</p>
                <h2 class="people-section__heading">The best work happens when people feel valued.</h2>
                <figure class="people-feature">
                    <div class="people-feature__grid">
                        <picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/img/pages/about-me/story/foundation-expo.webp"><img src="/assets/img/pages/about-me/story/foundation-expo.jpg" width="1200" height="800" alt="Dwayne with three Foundation Commerce colleagues at the Foundation stand, all in Foundation T-shirts" loading="lazy" /></picture>
                        <picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/img/pages/about-me/story/partner-community.webp"><img src="/assets/img/pages/about-me/story/partner-community.jpg" width="1200" height="800" alt="Dwayne kneeling at the front of a large group of Hyvä partners at the Hyvä and Hypernode stand" loading="lazy" /></picture>
                    </div>
                    <figcaption class="about-story__caption">With the Foundation team and fellow Hyv&auml; partners at eCommerce Expo London 2026. Photos: Hyv&auml;</figcaption>
                </figure>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

</main>

<%- include("../partials/footer") %>
</body>
</html>
